A quick-reference guide for embedding, routing, and sizing images in web projects.
1. Basic syntax
- The <img> tag is self-closing(doesn't need a closing (</img> tag ) and requires two core attributes:
<img src="path_to_image.jpg" alt="Clear text description of the image">
 -> src(source): The file path telling the browser where to find the image.
-> alt (Alternative Text): Text displayed if the image fails to load; crucial for SEO and screen readers.
2. File Directory Paths
 Use relative notation to point the src attribute to the correct folder location:
->  ./image.png(current directory): Links to an image located in the exact same folder as your HTML file.
->   ../image.png (Parent Directory): Moves up one folder level to look for the image.
->    /images/image.png (root directory): start looking from the absolute top-level folder of your project repository.

